WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:03.750
- The only brownies I ever
ate growing up were these.

00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:06.510
It's the recipe my mom would
make to bring to PTA meetings.

00:00:06.510 --> 00:00:08.270
We had it for dessert at dinner parties,

00:00:08.270 --> 00:00:11.260
it's like, these brownies
are always a hit.

00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:12.740
Hi, I'm Alexis deBoschnek

00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:14.280
and today, I'm gonna show you how to make

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:16.240
my One-Bowl Fudgy Brownie recipe

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:19.130
for my upcoming cookbook,
"To the Last Bite".

00:00:19.130 --> 00:00:20.850
There's walnuts, there's salt,

00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:25.233
it's fudgy, sweet, savory,
it's really my perfect brownie.

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:28.810
First, I like to line the
pan with parchment paper,

00:00:28.810 --> 00:00:31.310
just so it's easy to bring
them out of the tray.

00:00:31.310 --> 00:00:33.790
Place the chocolate in
a microwave safe bowl

00:00:33.790 --> 00:00:36.180
and microwave it in 30-second intervals,

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:38.720
just until the chocolate's melted.

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:40.110
Now that the chocolate's melted,

00:00:40.110 --> 00:00:41.350
you're gonna add the melted butter

00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:44.036
and use a hand mixer to
beat until just combined.

00:00:44.036 --> 00:00:48.100
(lighthearted guitar music)

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:51.090
Now, add the sugar, combine again.

00:00:51.090 --> 00:00:54.080
Alternatively, you can
do this in a stand mixer

00:00:54.080 --> 00:00:55.450
or even by hand.

00:00:55.450 --> 00:00:57.333
Add vanilla extract, then eggs.

00:00:57.333 --> 00:01:00.080
(lighthearted guitar music)

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:02.408
And once again, beat until combined.

00:01:02.408 --> 00:01:06.630
(lighthearted guitar music)

00:01:06.630 --> 00:01:11.090
Add kosher salt, and flour,
and just carefully combine,

00:01:11.090 --> 00:01:13.850
making sure not to over beat the batter.

00:01:13.850 --> 00:01:16.070
These are really fudgy brownies.

00:01:16.070 --> 00:01:18.350
They've got an incredible texture.

00:01:18.350 --> 00:01:20.310
I had some walnuts for a bit of crunch

00:01:20.310 --> 00:01:21.860
and some flaky sea salt on top

00:01:21.860 --> 00:01:23.100
so you're really balancing

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:26.540
that sweet, savory flavor profile.

00:01:26.540 --> 00:01:28.650
But if you don't like
walnuts or have an allergy,

00:01:28.650 --> 00:01:30.670
you can use another type of nut.

00:01:30.670 --> 00:01:32.510
Pour the brownie batter into the pan

00:01:32.510 --> 00:01:34.794
and then use a spatula to smooth the top.

00:01:34.794 --> 00:01:37.080
(lighthearted guitar music)

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:40.075
Pop them in the oven, and they're
gonna bake for 25 minutes.

00:01:40.075 --> 00:01:43.460
(lighthearted guitar music)

00:01:43.460 --> 00:01:46.300
I like to top my brownies
with some flaky sea salt,

00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:48.350
but it's really important
that you let them cool

00:01:48.350 --> 00:01:50.720
for at least 30 minutes.

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:52.503
You just lift them out of the pan,

00:01:52.503 --> 00:01:53.930
(lighthearted guitar music)

00:01:53.930 --> 00:01:55.663
slice away, and enjoy.

00:01:56.500 --> 00:01:58.240
One of the reasons I love these brownies

00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:00.400
is that it's all done in one bowl.

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:04.200
Easy to make, easy cleanup,
what could be better than that?

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:06.827
This is just one recipe
in my upcoming cookbook,

00:02:06.827 --> 00:02:07.840
"To the Last Bite".

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:11.290
It comes out April 19th and
there's over a hundred recipes,

00:02:11.290 --> 00:02:13.610
many of which were
inspired by my childhood,

00:02:13.610 --> 00:02:14.735
like these brownies.

00:02:14.735 --> 00:02:18.402
(lighthearted guitar music)

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:21.810
Mmm.

00:02:21.810 --> 00:02:23.370
They're fudgy, they're sweet,

00:02:23.370 --> 00:02:25.710
they're salty, the perfect texture.

00:02:25.710 --> 00:02:27.842
I really hope you make these brownies.

00:02:27.842 --> 00:02:31.390
(lighthearted guitar music)

00:02:31.390 --> 00:02:32.972
- [Tasty] Oh, yes!

00:02:32.972 --> 00:02:36.639
(lighthearted guitar music)

